                "text": ":loud_sound: Just 1 week to go! Save your spot now!\n\n𝐏𝐫𝐨𝐟.\/𝐃𝐫. 𝐉𝐢𝐧𝐱𝐢𝐚 𝐇𝐮𝐚𝐧𝐠 and her team did a survey of East Asia to see how the UNESCO Open Science Recommendations are being implemented regionally. Interested in seeing the results?\n\nJoin us for 𝐄𝐩𝐢𝐬𝐨𝐝𝐞 𝟓: 𝐂𝐨𝐧𝐧𝐞𝐜𝐭𝐢𝐧𝐠 𝐒𝐜𝐢𝐞𝐧𝐜𝐞 𝐀𝐜𝐫𝐨𝐬𝐬 𝐁𝐨𝐫𝐝𝐞𝐫𝐬: 𝐑𝐞𝐚𝐥𝐢𝐬𝐢𝐧𝐠 𝐔𝐍𝐄𝐒𝐂𝐎’𝐬 𝐎𝐩𝐞𝐧 𝐒𝐜𝐢𝐞𝐧𝐜𝐞 𝐑𝐞𝐜𝐨𝐦𝐦𝐞𝐧𝐝𝐚𝐭𝐢𝐨𝐧𝐬 of the 𝑹𝒆𝒔𝒆𝒂𝒓𝒄𝒉 𝑺𝒐𝒇𝒕𝒘𝒂𝒓𝒆 𝒂𝒏𝒅 𝑵𝑹𝑬𝑵𝒔 𝒊𝒏 𝑨𝒔𝒊𝒂 Community Conversation series as she shares practical insights from the work her team did at the Open Science Research Center of the National Science Library of Chinese Academy of Sciences (NSLC), Beijing, China along with UNESCO.\n\n𝐇𝐨𝐰 𝐭𝐨 𝐣𝐨𝐢𝐧?\nHere’s the link to get the joining details in your inbox:\n:point_right: 𝐑𝐞𝐠𝐢𝐬𝐭𝐞𝐫 𝐡𝐞𝐫𝐞: <https:\/\/lnkd.in\/dcCppYxA> \n\n:spiral_calendar_pad: 𝐃𝐚𝐭𝐞: 18 August 2026\n:alarm_clock: 𝐓𝐢𝐦𝐞: 06:00 - 07:00 UTC \n:round_pushpin: 𝐖𝐡𝐞𝐫𝐞: Online\n:admission_tickets: 𝐂𝐨𝐬𝐭: Free and open to all\n\n:link: Event details: <https:\/\/lnkd.in\/dnpkG-6X>\n\n#ResearchSoftware #Data #OpenData #OpenScience #RSE #RSEAsia #Webinar #ResearchInfrastructure #library #data #OpenScienceImplementation #OSI #UNESCO #Recommendations #2021 #leadership",
